From 423f5843bf0db281c5b27b5c4063816e7e37e570 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:47:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] microblaze: include elfos.h [PR target/101766]

microblaze.h defines OBJECT_FORMAT_ELF, so __has_attribute (symver) is
true, but no MicroBlaze configuration includes elfos.h, so
ASM_OUTPUT_SYMVER_DIRECTIVE is missing and using the attribute fails
with "symver is only supported on ELF platforms".  __ELF__ is not
defined either.  microblaze.h carries its own copies of much of
elfos.h instead.

Add elfos.h to tm_file for microblaze*-*-elf, microblaze*-*-rtems* and
microblaze*-*-linux*, ahead of microblaze.h, as lm32 does, so that
microblaze.h overrides it.  Remove the definitions elfos.h now
provides, and #undef the ones MicroBlaze keeps: .weakext, .rodata as a
directive, $-prefixed internal labels, .space, .asciz, the
MAX_OFILE_ALIGNMENT limit, the "ax" flags on .init and .fini, the
empty ASM_DECLARE_FUNCTION_NAME (microblaze_function_prologue emits
the label), and the plain .rodata section for constant-pool entries.
microblaze_declare_object is no longer used and goes.

The generated code is unchanged apart from __ELF__, .symver, and the
.size of an object with an initialized flexible array member, which
elfos.h takes from DECL_SIZE_UNIT and MicroBlaze took from the type
(4 rather than 12 for struct { int n; int a[]; } x = { 2, { 3, 4 } }).
The assembly also gains .file, .globl for libcalls and some spacing
changes, none of which changes the object file.  I compared the objects
for the 1678 gcc.c-torture/execute tests that compile as they are, at
-O2, both byte orders, for microblaze-elf (also with -fPIC) and
microblaze-rtems: only the two tests with such initializers,
20010924-1.c and pr33382.c, differ.

Tested on microblaze-elf (big-endian) with gcc.target/microblaze,
gcc.c-torture/execute and gcc.dg/ipa/symver1.c under QEMU.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

	PR target/101766

gcc/ChangeLog:

	* config.gcc (microblaze*-linux*, microblaze*-*-rtems*)
	(microblaze*-*-elf): Add elfos.h to tm_file.
	* config/microblaze/microblaze.h (OBJECT_FORMAT_ELF)
	(DWARF2_DEBUGGING_INFO, PREFERRED_DEBUGGING_TYPE)
	(ASCII_DATA_ASM_OP, TYPE_ASM_OP, SIZE_ASM_OP, COMMON_ASM_OP)
	(TYPE_OPERAND_FMT, ASM_DECLARE_OBJECT_NAME)
	(ASM_FINISH_DECLARE_OBJECT, MAKE_DECL_ONE_ONLY)
	(TARGET_ASM_NAMED_SECTION, TARGET_LIBC_HAS_FUNCTION): Remove;
	elfos.h defines them.
	(ASM_DECLARE_FUNCTION_NAME, ASM_GENERATE_INTERNAL_LABEL)
	(ASM_OUTPUT_SKIP, STRING_ASM_OP, MAX_OFILE_ALIGNMENT)
	(ASM_WEAKEN_LABEL, READONLY_DATA_SECTION_ASM_OP)
	(INIT_SECTION_ASM_OP, FINI_SECTION_ASM_OP): Undefine elfos.h's
	definition first.
	(TARGET_ASM_SELECT_RTX_SECTION): Undefine.
	* config/microblaze/microblaze.cc (microblaze_declare_object):
	Remove.
	* config/microblaze/microblaze-protos.h
	(microblaze_declare_object): Remove.

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	PR target/101766
	* gcc.target/microblaze/others/elf-size-flex.c: New test.
	* gcc.target/microblaze/others/elf-symver.c: New test.
